Ant is a MuJoCo environment with a 3D four-legged robot. The goal is to walk forward (in the x-direction) as fast as possible while staying healthy (not falling over).
The state is a vector of 27 elements:
- state[0]: z-coordinate (height) of the torso (0.2 to 1.0 m — healthy range)
- state[1]: w-component of the torso quaternion orientation
- state[2]: x-component of the torso quaternion orientation
- state[3]: y-component of the torso quaternion orientation
- state[4]: z-component of the torso quaternion orientation (not included; only 3 of 4 quaternion components)
- state[5-12]: angles of the 8 hip/ankle joints
- state[13]: x-velocity of the torso (forward speed)
- state[14]: y-velocity of the torso
- state[15]: z-velocity of the torso
- state[16]: roll angular velocity
- state[17]: pitch angular velocity
- state[18]: yaw angular velocity
- state[19-26]: angular velocities of the 8 joints
The action space is a vector of 8 float numbers representing torques applied to the 8 joints (-1 to 1 N).
The policy is a linear policy with 224 parameters and works as follows:
action = state @ W + b, where
state = [state[0], ..., state[26]]
W is a 27×8 matrix:
params[0..7]    = W[0,:]   (weights for state[0] = torso height)
params[8..15]   = W[1,:]   (weights for state[1])
params[16..23]  = W[2,:]   (weights for state[2])
params[24..31]  = W[3,:]   (weights for state[3])
params[32..39]  = W[4,:]   (weights for state[4])
params[40..47]  = W[5,:]   (weights for state[5])
params[48..55]  = W[6,:]   (weights for state[6])
params[56..63]  = W[7,:]   (weights for state[7])
params[64..71]  = W[8,:]   (weights for state[8])
params[72..79]  = W[9,:]   (weights for state[9])
params[80..87]  = W[10,:]  (weights for state[10])
params[88..95]  = W[11,:]  (weights for state[11])
params[96..103] = W[12,:]  (weights for state[12])
params[104..111]= W[13,:]  (weights for state[13] = x-velocity)
params[112..119]= W[14,:]  (weights for state[14] = y-velocity)
params[120..127]= W[15,:]  (weights for state[15] = z-velocity)
params[128..135]= W[16,:]  (weights for state[16])
params[136..143]= W[17,:]  (weights for state[17])
params[144..151]= W[18,:]  (weights for state[18])
params[152..159]= W[19,:]  (weights for state[19])
params[160..167]= W[20,:]  (weights for state[20])
params[168..175]= W[21,:]  (weights for state[21])
params[176..183]= W[22,:]  (weights for state[22])
params[184..191]= W[23,:]  (weights for state[23])
params[192..199]= W[24,:]  (weights for state[24])
params[200..207]= W[25,:]  (weights for state[25])
params[208..215]= W[26,:]  (weights for state[26])
b = [params[216], params[217], params[218], params[219], params[220], params[221], params[222], params[223]]
The reward function:
reward = healthy_reward + forward_reward - ctrl_cost - contact_cost
where:
- healthy_reward = 1.0 per step when the ant is healthy
- forward_reward = x-velocity
- ctrl_cost = 0.5 * sum(action^2)
- contact_cost = 0.5e-3 * sum(contact_forces^2), clipped
The ant is healthy if the z-coordinate (height) of the torso is between 0.2 and 1.0. The episode ends early if the ant falls over. Good policies achieve rewards of 3000–6000+ per episode.
